{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error. The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item. For source identities the application can supply independently, implement `source_address` to recover the project-relative outline address from the domain identity. Other identities return `None`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap in `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`. Each obligation maps to a test with assertions:\n\n- **Mapping returns `NodeData` and the SDK interns it.**\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` maps `src/parser.rs` + `impl[Parser]/fn[parse]` through `source_node`. It asserts that `source_address` returns the same address.\n  - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` shows the mapped identity, `source-node`, is interned. The recorded dependency is `Dependency::Node(cache.intern_node(\"source-node\"), …)`.\n  - `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` asserts dependencies on interned `TestNode{id:7/8/9}`. It also asserts that `source_node` received `visible/selected.txt` with an empty selector.\n- **Unsupported or invalid address returns an error.**\n  - The Habeas test rejects `../outside.rs`, `/absolute.rs`, the malformed selector `fn[` and the empty path. It also asserts `source_address` is `None` for the matching input selectors.\n  - The direct-read test uses an `unknown.txt` path and an unknown `line[unknown]` selector. It asserts the \"unsupported source item\" error, no recorded dependencies and no reads.\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled]` asserts the default `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`.\n  - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[agent_node_addresses_round_trip_and_reject_inconsistent_identities_before_reads]` rejects absent files and absent selectors. It asserts that no reads happen.\n- **The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item.** The configured-agent test uses a `TestDomain` with no `source_address` override. It still reads a listed `node` id back through `read_node`. The reply is the snapshot text, so the retained address is what resolves the identity. The `source-node` identity in the direct-read test has no `#` and so also has no recoverable address; it is read through the same retained mapping.\n- **`source_address` recovers the address for identities the application can supply, and other identities return `None`.**\n  - The Habeas test round-trips a method address. It asserts `None` for all six Habeas node kinds (requirement, reference set, selection, definition, source, site review).\n  - The contracts test asserts `source_address(&Node(1))` is `None` for the default domain.\n  - The `agent_node_addresses…` test round-trips `parser.rs#impl[Parser]` through `data`, `node` and `path` forms and rejects inconsistent combinations.\n\nThe remaining `{test}` markers on these tests are marked correctly for this requirement. I relied on the `Domain::source_address` and `intern_source` implementation only to confirm the retention mechanism.",
